### What is CountDownLatch?

You create it with a count. `await()` blocks until zero. `countDown()` decrements by one.

### How does the startup gate pattern work?

Every worker calls `startGate.await()` at the top. The coordinator calls `countDown()` once to fire the starting gun.

```java
CountDownLatch startGate = new CountDownLatch(1);
ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);

for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    pool.submit(() -> {
        startGate.await();  // all 10 block here
        doSettlement();
        return null;
    });
}

startGate.countDown();  // fire the starting gun: all 10 begin together
```

### How does the completion gate pattern work?

The count equals the number of workers. Each worker counts down in a finally block.

```java
CountDownLatch doneGate = new CountDownLatch(10);

for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    pool.submit(() -> {
        try {
            doSettlement();
        } finally {
            doneGate.countDown();  // always in finally!
        }
    });
}

doneGate.await();  // coordinator blocks until all 10 finish
System.out.println("All settlements complete.");
```

### Why must countDown be in a finally block?

If a worker crashes before decrementing, the coordinator waits forever.

### How do you prevent infinite waiting?

Use the timed variant:

```java
boolean allDone = doneGate.await(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
if (!allDone) {
    System.err.println("Timeout: not all workers finished.");
}
```

### Why can a latch not be reset?

Once the count hits zero it stays zero forever. For repeated rendezvous use `CyclicBarrier` (automatic reset) or `Phaser` (dynamic registration).

| Feature | CountDownLatch | CyclicBarrier | Phaser |
|---------|---------------|---------------|--------|
| Reset | No | Automatic | Automatic |
| Dynamic parties | No | No | Yes |
| Action on trip | No | Optional Runnable | Yes |
| Use case | One-time event | Repeated rounds | Dynamic phases |

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- Can multiple threads call countDown on the same latch?
- What happens if you call countDown more times than the initial count?
- How does CyclicBarrier handle a broken barrier?
